  "limits": [
    "The sweep finds only a second 8-K or 8-K/A filed on the same calendar date. A competing item bundled into the candidate's own filing (an extra Item beyond 2.02 and 9.01), or announced by a wire release with no 8-K, is invisible to it: Milestone 2 step 3's ALKT exclusion (a $400 million acquisition announced in the same minute as the earnings release) was found by reading the filing, not by this kind of sweep.",
    "It tests the filing date, not the reaction day: an after-hours release on day D reacts on the next session, so a filing on that next day is on the reaction day. The policy's own text speaks of the same calendar day as the earnings anchor, and this sweep follows it; the filings within three days are listed below so the content review can look at them.",
    "It says nothing about whether any candidate is an earnings-results release, its first-public timing, its identity or its corporate actions: those are the eligibility review and the owner's attestations."
